WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:02.270
- So you're in the new
live action "Cinderella"

00:00:02.270 --> 00:00:05.090
which I am so excited to see.

00:00:05.090 --> 00:00:07.310
And you play a version
of the Fairy Godmother.

00:00:07.310 --> 00:00:08.620
Will you tell us more about that?

00:00:08.620 --> 00:00:10.720
- Yeah, you know.

00:00:10.720 --> 00:00:15.580
They called and they asked me
to play the Fairy Godmuvva,

00:00:15.580 --> 00:00:20.520
as I call
him/her/they/them/she/it, whatever.

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:25.520
And you know, all I could think was that,

00:00:25.577 --> 00:00:28.090
"You're asking me to play
the Whitney Houston part?"

00:00:28.090 --> 00:00:31.056
- I love that you know
that version. (laughing)

00:00:31.056 --> 00:00:32.320
And Brandi.
- Wait, you're asking me

00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:34.354
to play the Whitney Houston part?

00:00:34.354 --> 00:00:36.069
♪ Impossible ♪

00:00:36.069 --> 00:00:38.796
Like I was like, (screaming).

00:00:38.796 --> 00:00:39.630
Yes, of course!

00:00:39.630 --> 00:00:41.850
What I love about it though,

00:00:41.850 --> 00:00:44.000
what I love about the position

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:48.790
is that it really speaks to my brand,

00:00:48.790 --> 00:00:50.430
for lack of a better word,

00:00:50.430 --> 00:00:54.950
which is about challenging

00:00:54.950 --> 00:00:58.190
gender norms and stereotypes.

00:00:58.190 --> 00:01:00.900
What does it mean to be a man?

00:01:00.900 --> 00:01:04.740
What is masculinity exactly?

00:01:04.740 --> 00:01:07.950
And why do we, in this culture,

00:01:07.950 --> 00:01:12.950
think that masculine is
better than feminine?

00:01:13.760 --> 00:01:17.090
I say, when I was trying to live up

00:01:17.090 --> 00:01:19.253
to the expectations of others,

00:01:20.450 --> 00:01:24.620
I was broke and bankrupt and jobless.

00:01:24.620 --> 00:01:28.260
When I chose myself, here we are.

00:01:28.260 --> 00:01:29.460
- [Kelly] Yeah, I agree.

